        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <img src="https://edd.ca.gov/siteassets/images/NewsletterBlogBanner_3_V3.jpeg" alt="Test" style="text-align: center; width: 100%; margin-right: 1px; margin-bottom: 3px; margin-left: 1px;" /><br /><br /><strong>THIS IS A RE-ADVERTISEMENT, IF YOU PREVIOUSLY APPLIED, YOU DO NOT HAVE TO RE-APPLY.</strong><br /><br /><strong>THIS POSITION MAY BE ELIGIBLE FOR A HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE. THE AMOUNT OF TELEWORK IS AT THE DISCRETION OF THE DEPARTMENT AND IS SUBJECT TO CHANGE AS BUSINESS NEEDS ARISE.</strong><br /><p><strong>DIS I FOT:</strong><br />Under close supervision, the Field Office Trainer (FOT) assists with training of newly hired Disability Insurance Program Representatives (DIPRs) and newly hired support staff; assists with providing refresher training for all staff. Works with the Training and Program Development Unit (TPDU) and the Management and Staff Development Unit (MSDU) to assess issues and develop solutions to meet training needs. Interacts with trainees, other FOTs, on-the-job trainers, FO staff, management, and the Disability Insurance (DI) Branch Training Section staff effectively.</p><p>The incumbent contributes toward the growth of the Branch into a customer-focused service organization by following and applying DI Branch cultural principles. The incumbent is required to have knowledge of the principles of the DI Branch program and protect program integrity by identifying and reporting any suspected fraudulent claims and/or activities.</p><p><strong>DIS II FOT:</strong><br />Under minimal supervision, the Field Office Trainer (FOT) provides training to newly hired Disability Insurance Program Representatives (DIPRs) and newly hired support staff; provides refresher training for all staff. Works with the Training and Program Development Unit (TPDU) and the Management and Staff Development Unit (MSDU) to assess issues and develop solutions to meet training needs. Interacts with trainees, other FOTs, on-the-job trainers, FO staff, management, and the Disability Insurance (DI) BranchTraining Section staff effectively.</p><p>The incumbent contributes toward the growth of the DI Branch into a customer-focused service organization by following and applying DI Branch cultural principles. The incumbent is required to have knowledge of the principles of the DI Branch program and protect program integrity by identifying and reporting any suspected fraudulent claims and/or activities.<br /><br />Position&nbsp;exists at  9246 Lightwave Ave, Bld A, Ste 300<br />San Diego CA 92123</p><ul></ul><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><div><ul></ul></div><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26254354&name=212.9218-9227.FOT.0826.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Visa Sponsorship</span></p><p>This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the US without the need for visa sponsorship by the start date of employment.<br />  </p>
                </p>
            
